pull.body:
Introduce a new field named `detailed` in RPC `getnettotals` to retrieve traffic bytes and count of messages broken down by:
* direction (sent or received)
* network (ipv4, tor, etc)
* connection type (outbound-full-relay, block-relay-only, etc)
* message type (verack, ping, etc)

Implements: https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/26337 Add per message stats to getnettotals rpc

---

Examples:

<details>
<summary>Group by direction (sum network, connection type, message type)</summary>

```
$ bitcoin-cli getnettotals | jq '.detailed | map_values([.[][][]] | { bytes: (map(.bytes) | add), count: (map(.count) | add) })'
{
  "recv": {
    "bytes": 288580402,
    "count": 562224
  },
  "sent": {
    "bytes": 11514028329,
    "count": 715094
  }
}
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>Group by network (sum direction, connection type, message type)</summary>

```
$ bitcoin-cli getnettotals | jq '
    [.detailed[] | to_entries[] | {key, value: [.value[][]]}]
    | group_by(.key)
    | map({
        key: .[0].key,
        value: ([.[].value[]] | { bytes: (map(.bytes) | add), count: (map(.count) | add) })
      })
    | sort_by(-.value.bytes)
    | from_entries
'

{
  "ipv4": {
    "bytes": 13195416760,
    "count": 689590
  },
  "ipv6": {
    "bytes": 850168762,
    "count": 187587
  },
  "onion": {
    "bytes": 516511904,
    "count": 378875
  },
  "i2p": {
    "bytes": 128190870,
    "count": 217514
  }
}
```
</details>

